<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system on Thursday via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements, the New York Fed confirmed.</p>
<p>The RPs were generally expected.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-5/8 percent when the Fed entered the open market, above the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target rate.</p>
<p>(( -- Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
